      "mergedPostDetails": "This is with the non-beta 3.5.2 build of the SDK. Anything that is listed in the Head Chop component will counter scale and offset those bones for the first frame in the personal or face mirror (have not tested in world mirrors). If the world is extremely optimized and giving you low frame times, it may happen too fast to be visible. \n\nIt seems like the counter scaling and offsets are being done before it checks if it is in the mirror world, if they were applied after this check there wouldn't be a visible issue.\n\nThe attached GIF has the two ears set to the head chop component.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Head chop counter scales in mirror",
